<h1>Data Deletion Instructions</h1>
<p class="updated">Last updated: 18 November 2026</p>

<p>The <strong>Page Manager</strong> application is a private tool operated by Imtiaz Ahmad ("the Operator") to publish and schedule video content to Facebook Pages that the Operator owns and administers. The App is used only by the Operator, with the Operator's own Facebook account, and does not collect data from the public.</p>

<h2>What data exists</h2>
<p>The App stores only the Operator's own access tokens and publishing records, kept in the Operator's private Google Drive storage. The App does not maintain accounts or profiles for any other person.</p>

<h2>How to request deletion</h2>
<p>Anyone who believes the App holds data relating to them may request its deletion in either of two ways:</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>By email:</strong> send a request to <strong>imtiazahmad54544@gmail.com</strong> with the subject "Data Deletion Request". The request will be confirmed by reply, and all related data held by the App will be permanently deleted within 30 days (normally much sooner).</li>
  <li><strong>Through Facebook:</strong> go to Facebook <em>Settings &rarr; Business integrations</em> (or <em>Settings &rarr; Apps and websites</em>), select the Page Manager app, and choose <em>Remove</em>. This immediately revokes the App's access; any tokens held by the App for that connection will then be deleted from the Operator's storage.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Confirmation</h2>
<p>After a deletion request is completed, the Operator will confirm completion by email to the address the request was sent from.</p>
